You can define a method foosBuilder(Comparator<T>) that returns the associated builder type for that sorted collection (ie. SortedSet or SortedMap) that uses given comparator to sort added values. In this example, we have an ImmutableSortedSet<String> which can be built using the countriesBuilder(Comparatror<String>) method:

```
@AutoValue
public abstract class Animal {
  public abstract ImmutableSortedSet<String> countries();

  public static Builder builder() {
    return new AutoValue_Animal.Builder();
  }

  @AutoValue.Builder
  public abstract static class Builder {
    public abstract ImmutableSortedSet.Builder<String> countriesBuilder(Comparator<String> comparator);
    public abstract Animal build();
  }
}
```

See https://github.com/caddyserver/caddy/pull/3990 for the change in Caddy that makes this possible.

To try this, I had to build this from a temp directory with a `go.mod` like this, to replace both the caddy and caddy-exec modules with local copies, so you would need to do the same to try it out until the upstream PR is merged/released.

```
module caddy

go 1.15

replace github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2 => ../caddy

replace github.com/abiosoft/caddy-exec => ../caddy-exec

require (
        github.com/abiosoft/caddy-exec v0.0.0-00010101000000-000000000000
        github.com/caddyserver/caddy/v2 v2.3.0
)
```

Also updated the `go.mod` to the latest versions.

Here's the adapt:

Caddyfile
```
{
        exec {
                command curl.exe "https://google.com" {
                        at startup
                }
                command echo {
                        args "foobar"
                        at startup
                }
                command hugo {
                        args "generate" "--destination=/home/user/site/public"
                        directory /foo/bar
                        at startup
                        foreground
                        timeout 10s
                }
        }
}
```

